Virtual thread 
On creation -> JVM creates a pool of platform thread with Stack 

On Execution -> Virtual thread mounts on platform thread .
  Carrier thread - platform threadexecuting Virtual thread 

On execution completetion -> unmounts virtual thread from  carrier thread 
    Carrier thread becomes platform thread available for other virtual thread to mount 
    Virtual thread available for garbage collection 

On execution waiting , Not able to progress execution 
      -> unmounts virtual thread from carrier thread + save state in head 
     Carrier thread becomes platform thread available for other virtual thread to mount 
    Virtual thread state gets saved in stack and instraction pointer for later execution 
    
On execution resume :
    JVM checks for available platform threads to amount the virtual thread 
    If all platform thread are unavailable 
      JVM unmounts one of the virtual thread and save state by stack and IP 
      JVM mounts the paused Virtual thread for completion 

Only CPU operations => Go ahead with normal thread 
  Virtual thread will only give an abstraction 
CPU + IO operation => When thread needs to wait , virtual thread are useful 

Issue : Virtual thread - JVM 21 to 23 
Thread Pining - when virtual thread gets stuck waiting on sync resource 
              and not getting unmounted from carrier thread 

Prior to J24,
 JVM tied object monitor to carrier thread 
       If virtual thread blocked while holding a object monitor inside synchronized 
       it would pin the carrier thread until operation completes 

JVM cannot suspend the thread safely when virtual thread calls native code ( JNI/Memory API)
    it causes pinning it to carrier 


Scenario 1:
Single threaded Web app listens http request and connects to DB to get results 
Consider: Single core 
Thread pool : 1 
Steps :
Parse the user request - non blocking 
Fetch data from DB - Blocking IO call --- Thread idle  
Send response back to user - non blocking 

Above is IO bound application in which most of time waiting / doing IO 
While waiting for IO operation other request will not be served 

Blocking IO - normal Thread :
public void handleRequest(HttpExchange exchange){
    Request request=parseUserRequest(exchange);
    Response data=readFromDataBase(request);
    sendPageToUser(data,exchange);
}
Blocking IO - Virtual Thread :
public void handleRequest(HttpExchange exchange){
    Request request=parseUserRequest(exchange);
    Response data=readFromDataBase(request); //No CPU resource wastage , No context switch 
    sendPageToUser(data,exchange);
}

